  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Following chromatogram was developed by adsorption of compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&#39; on a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> TLC glass plate. Retardation factor of the compound &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&#39; is _____&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0160_48d311135cfa.png\" style=\"width: 415px; height: 239px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0160_48d311135cfa.png\" style=\"width: 415px; height: 239px;\" /><br />From the above picture of chromatographic plate, retardation factor is:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>&#160;Distance moved by the substance from base line&#160;</mtext><mtext>&#160;Distance moved by the solvent from base line&#160;</mtext></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p>"
  }
}